a )(-3-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ 6+2\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -14 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 14}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =-7,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =2.$" 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446718 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1069 "q-36772" 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1072 #uuid "688b15c3-44c2-5c91-89ca-dd25252cd049" 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446737 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-11-\\lambda )-6\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ -33-3\\lambda +11\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+54 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +21 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={8}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =64-84 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $L$ does not have real eigenvalues." 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446738 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446723 13194139534980 17592186045417 true] [17592186446738 1069 "q-36781" 1319413953